      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reviewer": "Claude (session 01PK45rG), reviewing docs/evidence/expression/*_front.png directly",
      "notes": "VISUAL_FAIL, and it outranks 16/16 physical. WORKS: the blink is real and symmetric -- both upper lids visibly travel down over the sclera; nostril flare visibly widens the alar walls and wrinkles the nose; every expression reaches the screen. FAILS, none of which any current measurement can express: (1) 10_JAW_OPEN is the worst -- opening the mouth exposes a jagged white sheet where an arch should be and a pale wedge tearing down toward the chin. This is the skin-only facs_jawOpen dragging the lower face while the lower arch, which rides the jaw BONE, stays put. Predicted from the numbers (upper lip -0.0222 vs lower -0.0445, cosine +0.999); far worse in pixels than 'the teeth stay shut'. (2) REST does not seal -- the lips show a dark parted slit with red interior and a tooth at the right corner, on a pose whose whole job is a closed mouth. (3) The eyes never fully close at blink 1.0: slivers of sclera remain, because the globe protrudes past the lid plane. (4) Dark artifacts at the nose base in every frame. (5) A hard horizontal seam above the upper lip, visible in 05_NOSTRIL_FLARE. NEXT: drive the jaw BONE from facs_jawOpen (the lip_corner_*_wide driver pattern), then re-cut the lip seal at REST.",
      "rule": "VISUAL_FAIL outranks a passing physical gate. PENDING is not PASS."
    },
